    "title": "Gun, knife recovered from vehicle at Johnston High School - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Rachael Kauffman ,\n7 hours ago\nJOHNSTON, Iowa -- Johnston Community School District officials say a gun and knife were recovered from a vehicle at the high school.\nThe district says that just before noon on Thursday, the Johnston Police Department responded to a 911 call regarding Johnston High School. The school resource officer was already on site at the time of the call.\nDuring their investigation, Johnston officers recovered a knife and an unloaded gun from an unoccupied vehicle located in the south parking lot of the high school, according to district officials.\nPostal worker shot 2 colleagues at Des Moines post office before being detained, police say Authorities say it is believed to be an isolated incident, and there has been no information about any additional threats. The district says classes inside the high school continued and were not affected.\n\"JCSD continues our commitment to school safety and is taking this situation very seriously. We applaud our students and staff who continue to speak up and share information. We encourage everyone that when they see or hear something that is concerning, to call 911 or report it immediately to school staff,\" a news release from the district read.\nThe Johnston CSD and PD are working together to investigate this incident, including gathering surveillance information and witness statements. Officials say two students are being questioned.\nAuthorities say no further details about this incident are being released at this time.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to who13.com.\nAdd to Preferred Sources",
    "summary": "During their investigation, Johnston officers recovered a knife and an unloaded gun from an unoccupied vehicle located in the south parking lot of the high school, according to district officials. Postal worker shot 2 colleagues at Des Moines post office before being detained, police say Authorities say it is believed to be an isolated incident, and there has been no information about any additional threats. The district says classes inside the high school continued and were not affected.",
